Cys-SG to GAFF2 ligand junction (D0023, extended D0027).

ff19SB type S meets a GAFF2 carbon at the covalent bond and no force field
covers that pair. EVERY term below is taken from the GAFF2 parameter for the
same geometry with GAFF2's thioether sulfur `ss` in place of the protein's `S`.
That analogue is not a convenience: once Cys113 SG bonds the ligand it IS a
thioether sulfur (CB-S-C_lig), which is exactly what `ss` describes.

An earlier version of this file hand-picked analogues from parm19 and covered
only sp3 carbon (`c3`). Six of nine warhead classes attach through sp2 or
aromatic carbon, so 18 of 27 MM-GBSA builds failed. Deriving every term from one
source removes both the gap and the inconsistency.

Values below are verbatim from gaff2.dat; the source line is the `ss` form of
each name.

